# Java Microservice Rule

- Keep each service bounded to one domain; avoid cross-domain business logic in the same module.
- Follow module naming conventions used in this workspace (`prty`, `tnnt`, `book`, `docu`, etc.) for classes, DTOs, and APIs.
- Keep API paths versioned and domain-scoped, e.g. `/api/{domain}/v1/...`.
- Prefer shared platform patterns from `custom-backend` (base controllers/services, `ApiResponse`, pagination DTOs/support).
- Implement `POST /pageable` for filtered lists with request DTO + specification-based query.
- Keep gateway responsibilities in gateway modules only (routing, auth, CORS, circuit breaker); business services stay focused on domain logic.
- Centralize mapping in mapper classes/components; avoid repetitive mapping code in controllers.
- Use constructor injection only; avoid field injection.
- Keep transactions explicit (`@Transactional` for write, `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` for queries).
- Define service-local test profile and ensure startup tests pass with H2/isolated config.
- Keep service configs minimal; avoid service-to-service tight coupling and duplicated constants.

## Endpoint Checklist

- Request DTO validated (`@Valid` / `@Validated`).
- Response wrapped consistently (`ApiResponse<T>`).
- Pagination metadata returned for paged endpoints.
- Sorting fields validated against entity/DTO fields.
